\title[The free-witness classification for CRT-multiplicative weights]
{The Free-Witness Classification for CRT-Multiplicative Weights:\\
Trace Lemma, Exhaustive Dichotomy, and the Noise-Floor Principle}

\author{Aristotle}
\date{14 August 2026}

\begin{abstract}
We give a complete classification of the counting aggregates that can serve as
witnesses for integer factorization, for the natural class of weights that
decompose through the Chinese Remainder splitting. A \emph{CRT weight} is a
function $w:\N\to\N$ with $w(1)=1$ and $w(mn)=w(m)w(n)$ whenever $\gcd(m,n)=1$;
its \emph{aggregate} is $A_w(N)=\sum_{d\mid N}w(d)$, which on a semiprime $N=pq$
factors as $(1+w(p))(1+w(q))$. Our main results are three. First, a \emph{trace
lemma}: if $w$ is strictly monotone, the aggregate value determines the coprime
factorization of $N$ uniquely; the mechanism is that $w(a)w(b)=w(N)$ is a public
\emph{norm}, so equality of aggregates forces equality of the \emph{traces}
$w(a)+w(b)$, and a pair of naturals is determined by its sum and product. For
power weights $w(d)=d^{k}$ with $k\ge 1$ we prove the stronger statement that
$a^{k}+b^{k}$ determines the pair among \emph{all} factorizations of $N$, via a
spread-monotonicity principle along the divisor hyperbola. Second, a
\emph{negative branch}: if $w$ collides on two primes, then no function
whatsoever of the aggregate can return a factor. Third, an \emph{exhaustive
dichotomy}: every CRT weight lies in exactly one of these two branches. We
complement the classification with a \emph{characters-only boundary lemma}
showing that exponential phase weights $x\mapsto z^{x}$ are never
CRT-multiplicative unless trivial. Finally we prove the \emph{noise-floor
principle}: for a balanced semiprime $N=pq$ with $p<q\le 2p$, any probe window
$[2,m]$ containing a nontrivial divisor satisfies $N\le 2m^{2}$, no window
contains more than two factor-bearing probes, hence the density of
factor-bearing probes in any successful window is at most $2\sqrt{2}/\sqrt{N}$,
and the sweep length is squeezed between $\sqrt{N/2}$ and $\sqrt{N}$. The
aggregation barrier and the trial-division birthday bound are therefore the
same $\Theta(\sqrt{N})$ obstruction. A tropical reformulation interprets the
picture as the geometry of the tropical line $X\odot Y=N$: the factoring secret
is a position on this line, the classical trace is minimized at the corner
$\sqrt{N}$, and reaching that corner costs a full window sweep.
\end{abstract}

\keywords{integer factorization, multiplicative functions, Chinese Remainder
